    "full_story_part1_k1": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Work messages, news, videos, and that app you open without thinking. Your smartphone is already like a packed train at rush hour. What if someone said, “An AI pet is getting on, too”? And it is free. Your wallet nods. But your calendar looks away.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part1",
        "index": 1,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 45,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part1_k2": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Meta’s “Waddle World” is an AI pet app in the Philippines. It is free in app stores, and its official website says there is no subscription. The stamps you earn in the app cannot be bought with money. It is nice not to have to check a price list.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part1",
        "index": 2,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 49,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part1_k3": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "If you are thinking, “I’ll let my child play with it,” stop here. Both app stores say users must be 18 or older. This time, adults are asked if they want to welcome a pet.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part1",
        "index": 3,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 35,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part2_k1": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "The age labels are a little confusing. Apple says 18+, while Google Play gives it a 3+ content rating. But that rating does not say who can use the app. It does not mean, “OK from age three!” A content rating and the age needed to use an app are different things. Do not skip this just because the pet has a cute face.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part2",
        "index": 1,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 64,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part2_k2": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "If it costs nothing, you might next check how much storage space your phone has. Or maybe how much free time you have. The question is not, “Would I want it if I had to pay?” It is, “Do I want to spend a few minutes with this pet today, too?” Even though it is free, the test for letting it move in is surprisingly hard.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part2",
        "index": 2,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 66,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part2_k3": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "When it comes to usefulness, you can compare features side by side. But “I kind of want to see it” is hard to put in a chart. An AI pet may matter less to adults for what it can do. It may matter more if they want to make room for one during the gaps in a busy day.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part2",
        "index": 3,
        "count": 3,
        "words": 59,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part3_k1": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Still, it is too soon to get excited about future predictions. At the time of writing, no one had said when it would be available in Japan or other places. TechCrunch has suggested it may be an early step toward future devices like pets. But it does not say that any specific link has been confirmed.",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part3",
        "index": 1,
        "count": 2,
        "words": 56,
        "boundary_kind": "paragraph",
        "extra_pause_s": 0.2,
        "level": "a2",
        "std_slowdown_composition": "per_chunk_slowdown_then_pad_0.2s"
      }
    },
    "full_story_part3_k2": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "We still do not know if it will become a craze like Tamagotchi. Will “It’s free, so I’ll try it” turn into “I want to see this pet for a little while today, too”? A place to try it out and a seat kept for it every day are different. What is missing from an adult’s smartphone? A new resident? Or a little room in the day to care about someone?",
      "chunk_tts": {
        "planner_version": "chunk_tts_v1_x_paragraph_z_r1_20261025",
        "parent_id": "full_story_part3",
        "index": 2,
